  "slug": "agentic-operation-harness-54b9",
  "summary": "Three recent preprints present web and Bioconductor infrastructure for visualizing multilayered biological networks alongside omics measurements.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is interactive, accessible delivery of biological network analysis, realized either as browser-based applications or as R/Bioconductor data structures. Arena3D 3.0 is a web server for 3D visualization, analysis, annotation and sharing of multilayered networks imported from STRING and IntAct. NORMA 3.0 is a client-side rewrite for visualizing annotated networks, with group-aware layouts and multi-group node rendering. GraphExperiment extends SingleCellExperiment with an S4 class storing feature- and observation-level igraph networks synchronized with omics data. The dominant thread is therefore delivery and visualization of networks rather than a shared modality, and the NORMA summary does not indicate an omics link. What is new is the coupling of network topology with omics measurements in GraphExperiment, within a single Bioconductor container, while Arena3D and NORMA address network visualization and annotation. The summaries report no comparative benchmarks against existing tools.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-04"
}
